            <ArticleTitle>Stress-induced-antinociception and morphine sensitivity in mice following chronic treatment with anabolic/androgenic steroids.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>343-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In male mice treated chronically with anabolic/androgenic steroids, morphine produced changes in exploratory behaviour similar to those normally associated with anxiolytic drugs. In addition, steroid treatment attenuated opioid-mediated stress-induced antinociception.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
